{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 19, :comments ["<b>And of every living thing.</b> Rashi explains: to include demons. And it is found in Bereishit Rabbah: he [a demon] wanted to be called to enter the ark. Noah said to him: Go and seek your mate, for all who enter are male and female. He went and found Pachta, who is the one appointed over human beings to diminish them and reduce their property. He said to her: Will you marry me? She said to him: What will you give me if I marry you? He said to her: Whatever I acquire I will acquire for her. Immediately they entered the ark. And that is what people say: whatever one acquires, Pachta acquires. מסגל is from the language of סגולה."], :book :genesis, :voice :daat-zkenim, :lang :en, :chapter 6, :notes {0 "The Aramaic dialogue contains wordplay around the root נסב (to marry/take) that is preserved literally. The final proverb about Pachta is rendered hyper-literally; the underlying idiom means that whatever a person acquires, Pachta takes a share."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:05:07.985365826Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}